WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.275
Planning connects the observation objective to a safe and lawful method.

00:00:04.275 --> 00:00:08.980
Review the location, applicable rules, airspace, property access, terrain, obstacles,

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.540
people, nearby operations,

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.280
and current official restrictions before selecting a route or platform.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.230
Weather and lighting affect both aircraft safety and evidence quality.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.280
Wind, visibility, precipitation, temperature, glare, cloud cover,

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.280
and shadows may change during the mission.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.260
Select conditions that fit equipment limitations and the analytical question.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.235
Identify a controlled launch and recovery area when using a drone.

00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:33.130
Plan battery margins for takeoff, collection, return, contingencies, and landing.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:36.590
Do not build a route that depends on ideal endurance or an uninterrupted communication

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.230
link.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:41.520
Design a flight path or observation sequence that covers the authorized area with the

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.275
required angle and overlap.

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:46.275
Keep unnecessary private areas outside the frame where practical.

00:00:46.275 --> 00:00:49.280
Mark decision points for returning, landing, or ending collection.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.035
Prepare emergency options for changing weather, low battery, signal loss,

00:00:53.035 --> 00:00:56.869
people entering the area, navigation problems, or an unavailable recovery point.

00:00:56.869 --> 00:01:00.280
Brief crew communication and define who can call a stop.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:04.460
Document objective, location, crew, platform, permissions, official-source checks,

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:09.165
weather, lighting, hazards, controls, route, collection settings, and emergency actions.

00:01:09.165 --> 00:01:12.270
A written plan supports repeatability and later interpretation of the imagery.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.270
Review the plan immediately before collection because conditions can change.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:20.540
A route that was reasonable during desktop planning may become unsuitable when people,

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.000
vehicles, glare, wind, or temporary activity appear.
